            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <h2>When to Use This SOP</h2>
<p>This SOP applies to media buying teams managing Meta, TikTok, Google, and other major overseas ad platforms. Perform a complete audit at least once per week. For new platforms or newly launched accounts, increase the audit frequency to every 1-2 days during the first two weeks.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Pre-Audit Preparation</h2>
<p>Before starting the compliance audit, confirm the following:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Log into the main account dashboard</strong> and verify the operating account has Admin or Standard access (not Guest)</li>
<li><strong>Export this week's new creative assets</strong>, including images, videos, ad copy, and CTA button configurations</li>
<li><strong>Open the ad policy page</strong> (Meta Business Help Center / TikTok for Business Policy Center) and check for unread announcements</li>
<li><strong>Prepare the audit log template</strong>, using a tool like Feishu or Notion, and archive records after each audit</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h2>Step 1: Account Permission Audit</h2>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Time: ~10 minutes</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<ol>
<li>Go to Business Settings and review all linked accounts, checking bind dates and who added them</li>
<li>Remove access for departed employees or long-inactive users</li>
<li>Verify all payment methods linked to ad accounts are within their validity period</li>
<li>Check for unfamiliar IP login records — if any are found, immediately change passwords and enable two-factor authentication</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Warning Signs</strong>: Unknown admin accounts, payment methods showing "expiring soon" or "expired", login locations that don't match your team</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 2: Ad Creative Compliance Review</h2>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Time: ~20-30 minutes</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<h3>2.1 Text Layer</h3>
<ul>
<li>Avoid exaggerated therapeutic claims (e.g., "guaranteed cure", "miracle", "100% effective")</li>
<li>Health and financial products must comply with target country regulations (e.g., FDA disclaimers, financial product disclosures)</li>
<li>Avoid high-pressure sales language like "limited time" or "act now" unless you genuinely are running a time-limited promotion</li>
</ul>
<h3>2.2 Visual Assets</h3>
<ul>
<li>Ensure all people in images/videos are adults (any imagery involving children is prohibited)</li>
<li>Brand logos should appear correctly; competitor logos are prohibited</li>
<li>Verify the first 3 seconds of videos don't contain flashing effects that could trigger seizure warnings</li>
</ul>
<h3>2.3 Landing Page Consistency</h3>
<ul>
<li>Check that advertised discounts or gifts match the landing page exactly</li>
<li>Ensure CTA buttons align with ad copy promises</li>
<li>Confirm privacy policy and refund policy pages are accessible and functional</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 3: Policy Violation Screening</h2>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Time: ~15 minutes</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<ol>
<li>In the Ads Manager, filter for ads with "Disapproved" status</li>
<li>Read each rejection reason carefully — don't delete immediately; modify and resubmit instead</li>
<li>Check the notification center for any Account Quality rating drops</li>
<li>Review the Business Help Center for new policy updates affecting your industry</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Top 3 Common Rejection Reasons</strong>:<br />
- Misleading before/after comparison images<br />
- Undisclosed subscription-based billing models<br />
- Sensitive content (violence, gore, discriminatory elements)</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 4: Financial &amp; Recharge Risk Control</h2>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Time: ~10 minutes</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<ol>
<li>Compare actual spend against budget settings this week to identify overspend risks</li>
<li>Verify account balance is above the alert threshold (recommend triggering notifications when balance falls below 20% of daily spend)</li>
<li>Confirm the recharge account and ad account belong to the same entity to avoid tax review issues</li>
<li>If using a third-party agency for recharge, verify their invoice details match platform spending records</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h2>Recommended Audit Frequency</h2>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Operational Phase</th>
<th>Recommended Frequency</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>New account cold start (first 2 weeks)</td>
<td>Daily</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Stable running period</td>
<td>2x per week</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>High-consumption periods (sales events/holidays)</td>
<td>Daily + real-time monitoring</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Policy change periods (platform algorithm updates)</td>
<td>Special audit within 48 hours of announcement</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<hr />
<h2>Exception Handling Protocol</h2>
<p>When issues are found during audits, handle them by priority:</p>
<p><strong>P0 (Immediate Action)</strong>: Account permission anomalies, payment method failures, batch ad rejections → Pause relevant ads, contact platform support</p>
<p><strong>P1 (Within 24 Hours)</strong>: Individual creative violations, broken landing page links → Modify and resubmit</p>
<p><strong>P2 (Within This Week)</strong>: Policy updates requiring strategy adjustments, account quality drops → Adjust campaign structure, submit appeal materials</p>
<hr />
<h2>Quick Checklist</h2>
<ul>
<li>[ ] No unauthorized personnel in account permissions</li>
<li>[ ] Payment methods are within validity period</li>
<li>[ ] All new creatives from this week have been reviewed</li>
<li>[ ] No backlog of "Disapproved" ads</li>
<li>[ ] Landing pages match ad promises</li>
<li>[ ] Spend is aligned with budget (no anomalies)</li>
<li>[ ] No unread policy update announcements</li>
</ul>
<p>Print this checklist and keep it at your workstation, or create a tickable template in Feishu or Notion. Archive records after each completed audit.</p>
